# Deadlock — my summary (Bob)

Four things must all be true at once:
- resources that only one process can use at a time,
- processes keep what they have while asking for more,
- nobody can take a resource away from its holder,
- a cycle of processes each waiting on the next.

Kill any one of them and deadlock is impossible. In practice: acquire locks in one global order.

Detection = find a cycle in the wait-for graph. Avoidance = Banker's. Most OSes ignore it.
